rs/tcoxon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tcoxon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tcoxon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tcoxon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tcoxon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tcoxon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tcoxon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tcoxon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-24T16:40:55Z","updated_at":"2026-04-24T16:40:55Z","body":"I've also been hit hard by this upon upgrading to 4.6. My project has a lot of deeply nested resources, however I suspect the issue is not the number of resources, but the way in which `gather_resources` scans them. It doesn't make sense for it to take 10 minutes for the editor to update an icon when I can actually save all of those resources to disk in < 5 seconds. Something is behaving worse than O(N).\n\nA lot of my resources reference the same resources over and over. At a quick skim, gather_resources doesn't look like it checks if the resource has already been added to the list before recursively scanning it (and all resources it references) again.\n\nIf you have a reference graph like this example, although it's only 9 resources (A through I), the list will be 31 long, and all the properties of H and I will have been scanned 8 times each:\n\n<img width=\"320\" height=\"189\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/263ce353-5b1c-40f0-8175-50543c9a2968\" />\n\nIt gets a lot worse if you have more than 2 resources on each layer. My project has 8-64 resources on each of the last 3 layers 😆 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4314789844/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"